      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi saba, you are able to do this by:\n1. Keep a map to store the remote char info\n```\nself.characteristic_changed_map \u003d {remote_address: {char: changed, ...}, ...}\n```\n\n2. Register an observer `SendCharacteristicNotificationObserver` when Pandora GATT service init, and store every information when we are observing an `on_notify` callback. If there\u0027s a char in the map, set the future, else put a char future\ninto the map.\n\n3. When client calling WaitCharacteristicNotification, check the map. If there\u0027s\nno char in the map, then create a future put into map and then await on it, else\nreturn the response.\n\nPicture of the GATT architecture:\n\nFloss\n```\n                         ---conn 1--- remote1 gatt server\nGATT client1 callback1   ---conn 2--- remote2 gatt server\n                         ---conn 3--- remote3 gatt server\n```\n\nAndroid\n```\n               GATT instance1 client1 callback1 -conn 1--- remote1 gatt server\nGATT Manager1  GATT instance2 client2 callback2 -conn 2--- remote2 gatt server\n               GATT instance3 client3 callback3 -conn 3--- remote3 gatt server\n```\n\nPlease look at GattInstance.kt / android framework  v.s. floss framework for reference. Thanks.",
